# The API image (apps/api/Dockerfile) copies only the root manifests,
# apps/api, packages/shared and packages/mcp. Everything below is uploaded to
# the Fly builder on every deploy otherwise — the context was 4.1 GB (2.2 GB
# of it .claude/). Keep it lean. Do NOT ignore: pnpm-lock.yaml,
# pnpm-workspace.yaml, package.json, tsconfig.base.json, apps/api/**,
# packages/shared/**, packages/mcp/** — every packages/* the API depends on is
# COPYed by name in the Dockerfile and must stay out of this file.

.claude/
.git/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/.turbo/
.vercel/
**/.vercel/

# Sibling apps the API build never touches. Hand-listed, and it had stopped at
# the five apps that existed in July: membership, connections, my, models and
# website (some 13 MB of source and images) rode to the builder on every
# deploy until 2026-10-01. When an app is added, add it here.
apps/web/
apps/meet/
apps/thread/
apps/flow/
apps/pulse/
apps/membership/
apps/connections/
apps/my/
apps/models/
apps/website/

# Non-build material
docs/
supabase/
scratchpad/
e2e/
test-results/
playwright-report/
*.log
# Docker ignore patterns are relative to the CONTEXT ROOT, so a bare `.env`
# matched only /.env and left apps/api/.env in the context — and BuildKit
# never reads apps/api/.dockerignore, which has been decorative since it was
# written. The Dockerfile's COPY list is narrow enough that neither file
# reached the image, but the whole context is uploaded to the Fly remote
# builder, so the secrets crossed the wire on every deploy from a worktree
# (where they have to be copied in for `pnpm verify` to run). 2026-09-11.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
.DS_Store
